<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/hail-roof.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/hail-roof-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/hail-roof.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="683" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.15"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><a href="/what-we-handle/">Services</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><span aria-current="page">Roof &amp; Hail Damage Appraisal</span></nav><p class="kicker">Appraisal service</p><h1>Roof and Hail Damage Appraisal in Kansas</h1><p class="lede">Kansas sits in the heart of hail country. When an adjuster approves a repair and your roofer says the whole roof is gone, we look at every slope and settle the question with documentation.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-gold" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-line" href="/request-kansas-claim-review/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="hero-facts"><div><dt>Season</dt><dd>April–July peak</dd></div><div><dt>Common gap</dt><dd>Repair vs. replace</dd></div><div><dt>Includes</dt><dd>Soft metals &amp; elevations</dd></div></dl></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose">
<h2>Hail claims are scope fights</h2>
<p>The most common Kansas hail dispute is simple to describe: the insurer says three slopes are damaged and the rest can be repaired, and the homeowner’s contractor says the roof needs to be replaced. The answer turns on test squares, hit counts, the brittleness of older shingles, whether repairs can be made without damaging surrounding shingles, and whether replacement shingles match.</p>
<h2>What we document</h2>
<ul>
<li>Test squares on every slope, with hit counts photographed and marked.</li>
<li>Soft-metal indicators such as vents, flashing, gutters and downspouts that confirm hail size and direction.</li>
<li>Collateral damage to siding, window wraps, screens, AC fins, fences and painted surfaces.</li>
<li>Brittleness and repairability of the existing shingles.</li>
<li>Roof measurements, pitch, layers and decking condition.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Roof payment schedules and cosmetic exclusions</h2>
<p>Many Kansas policies now pay older roofs on a schedule tied to roof age, or exclude “cosmetic” damage to metal roofing. Those provisions change what you are paid, not how much damage exists. We value the damage accurately, and then the policy terms apply to that number. Try our <a href="/claim-calculators-kansas/roof-age-payment-schedule-calculator/">roof age payment schedule calculator</a> to see how a schedule affects your payout.</p>
<h2>Metal roofs, barns and outbuildings</h2>
<p>Ribbed metal on shops, barns and machine sheds is everywhere in rural Kansas. Hail can dent panels, crack paint and loosen fasteners. Whether that damage is covered depends on your form; how much it costs to fix does not, and that is where appraisal helps.</p>
<h2>Repeat storms and “old damage”</h2>
<p>When a roof has been hit by more than one storm, carriers sometimes attribute damage to an earlier date. Dated photos, weather data for your address and the condition of the impacts all help separate one storm from another.</p>

<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary><span>How many hits per test square does it take to replace a roof?</span><svg class="pl" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></summary><div class="a"><p>There is no single statewide rule. Carriers often use internal guidelines; panels look at the totality of the evidence, including repairability and matching.</p></div></details><details><summary><span>Does hail size matter?</span><svg class="pl" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></summary><div class="a"><p>Yes. Hail of about one inch and larger commonly damages asphalt shingles, but wind speed, shingle age and the angle of impact all matter.</p></div></details><details><summary><span>My roof is older. Is replacement still possible?</span><svg class="pl" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></summary><div class="a"><p>Possibly. Age affects depreciation and, under some policies, the payment schedule. It does not by itself mean the roof wasn’t damaged.</p></div></details></div>
<h2>Related services</h2><div class="rel-grid"><a href="/what-we-handle/tornado-wind-appraisal/"><small>Service</small><span>Tornado &amp; Straight-Line Wind Appraisal</span><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a href="/what-we-handle/ice-storm-freeze-appraisal/"><small>Service</small><span>Ice Storm &amp; Freeze Damage Appraisal</span><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a href="/what-we-handle/water-damage-appraisal/"><small>Service</small><span>Water Damage Appraisal</span><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div>
